From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 99995: let an MLD leg follow its client when it roams

An affiliated leg gets its BSSID in sta_table when it associates, and nothing
moves it when the MLD roams to another node. parse_associated_sta_mld_config()
rebuilds sm->stalist from the TLV, so affiliated_sta learns the new BSS, but the
struct sta the metrics path uses keeps the old one. The two then disagree about
the same leg.

handle_sta_link_metrics_response() compares the agent's per-link report against
that stale copy and drops the measurement.

Measured on hardware 2026-08-04, one MLO client steered from 4g to x8:

	affiliated_sta  96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 -> 0a:0c:43:26:a0:10   x8, where it is
	sta_table       96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 -> 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e   4g, where it was

	Ignore STA 96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 link-metrics with different bssid
	rcpi_steer: STA 96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 connected to 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e
	            on channel 1 has RCPI = 255

The agent measured it correctly - libwifi reported -26 dBm on the active link -
sent it, and the controller threw it away against its own stale copy. It then
steered on RCPI 255, which is the value that means "never measured". Nothing
warned, because from the controller's side both halves looked consistent.

The Associated STA MLD Configuration TLV is the agent stating which BSS each
leg is on right now. Let the leg follow it, and record the reporting node while
we are there.

This is the same shape as the two defects found earlier today: one piece of
state with two writers that do not agree. Here the fix is to give the stale
writer the authoritative value rather than to add a third.
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -4558,12 +4558,15 @@
  */
 static void parse_associated_sta_mld_config(struct node *n, struct cmdu_buff *cmdu)
 {
+	struct controller *c;
 	struct tlv *t;
 	int rem;
 
 	if (!n || !cmdu)
 		return;
 
+	c = n->cntlr;
+
 	rem = cmdu->datalen;
 	{
 		struct tlv *tt;
@@ -4659,6 +4662,46 @@
 			memcpy(as->macaddr, ent + 6, 6);
 			list_add_tail(&as->list, &sm->stalist);
 			sm->num_sta++;
+
+			/* A leg's entry in sta_table keeps the BSSID it had when
+			 * it associated, and nothing moves it when the MLD roams.
+			 * handle_sta_link_metrics_response() compares the agent's
+			 * per-link report against that stale value and throws the
+			 * measurement away. Measured 2026-08-04, one client steered
+			 * from 4g to x8:
+			 *
+			 *   affiliated_sta  96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 -> 0a:0c:43:26:a0:10  (x8, where it is)
+			 *   sta_table       96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 -> 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e  (4g, where it was)
+			 *
+			 *   Ignore STA 96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 link-metrics with different bssid
+			 *   rcpi_steer: STA 96:d4:32:c3:fc:c0 connected to 7e:04:1c:81:7c:2e
+			 *               ... has RCPI = 255
+			 *
+			 * So the agent measures the right thing, sends it, and the
+			 * controller discards it against its own stale copy - and
+			 * then steers on RCPI 255, which means "never measured".
+			 *
+			 * This TLV is the agent saying which BSS each leg is on now.
+			 * Let the leg follow it.
+			 */
+			if (c) {
+				struct sta *ls = cntlr_find_sta(c->sta_table,
+								as->macaddr);
+
+				if (ls && memcmp(ls->bssid, as->bssid, 6)) {
+					dbg("%s: leg " MACFMT " moved " MACFMT
+					    " -> " MACFMT "\n", __func__,
+					    MAC2STR(as->macaddr),
+					    MAC2STR(ls->bssid), MAC2STR(as->bssid));
+
+					memcpy(ls->bssid, as->bssid, 6);
+					if (ls->de_sta)
+						memcpy(ls->de_sta->bssid,
+						       as->bssid, 6);
+					memcpy(ls->agent_almacaddr,
+					       n->almacaddr, 6);
+				}
+			}
 		}
 
 		err("E2TRACE: STORED sta_mld " MACFMT " under ap_mld " MACFMT " links=%u\n",
